# entitlements_plist.xml — Example Entitlement Configuration

Secure baseline entitlements for a release-signed iOS app. Adapt `<TEAMID>` and bundle IDs; do not include wildcard keychain groups.

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Application identifier: auto-injected by signing; do not hand-edit -->
    <key>application-identifier</key>
    <string>&lt;TEAMID&gt;.com.example.app</string>

    <!-- Keychain: ONLY this app's access group — no wildcards -->
    <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>&lt;TEAMID&gt;.com.example.app</string>
    </array>

    <!-- Hardened runtime: enabled, no weakening flags -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.runtime</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- DO NOT set: allow-jit, allow-unsigned-executable-memory,
         allow-dyld-environment-variables, disable-library-validation,
         disable-executable-page-protection, debugger -->
    <!-- DO NOT set get-task-allow in release builds -->

    <!-- Network: only if the app accepts inbound connections -->
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- App Groups: one specific group, no wildcard -->
    <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>group.com.example.app</string>
    </array>

    <!-- Associated domains: explicit list only -->
    <key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
    <array>
        <string>applinks:example.com</string>
        <string>webcredentials:example.com</string>
    </array>

    <!-- Push notifications -->
    <key>aps-environment</key>
    <string>production</string>
</dict>
</plist>
```

Notes:
- The provisioning profile (embedded.mobileprovision) overrides/supersedes some of these; verify both with `ios-wizard static entitlements`.
- For keychain secrets, prefer `kSecAttrAccessibleWhenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly` at the API level over entitlement-level broadness.
